 " noted that this race was the first time in 12 years that all the world’s top swimmers had gathered at the Olympics. Otto was expected to be challenged by Americans " [:a {:href "/athletes/51218"} "Dara Torres"] ", winner of the 1987 Pan Pacs and 1988 world leader with 55.30, and " [:a {:href "/athletes/51088"} "Mitzi Kremer"] ", ranked third in the world in 1988. But they were non-factors, as Kremer did not make the final, and Torres would finish only seventh."] "\n\n" [:p {} "In the final, Otto was challenged by China’s surprising " [:a {:href "/athletes/46122"} "Zhuang Yong"] ", who had been ranked only 12th in the world in 1987 and was only ninth in 1988 coming into the Olympics. Otto won easily, Zhuang setting a PR of 55.50 for the silver, the first Olympic medal won by a Chinese swimmer. France’s " [:a {:href "/athletes/46766"} "Catherine Plewinski"] " was another surprise, winning the bronze medal, although she even admitted she did not think she could qualify for the A final. She had never medaled at an international meet before."] "\n"] [:table {:class "table table-striped"} [:thead {} [:tr {} [:th {} "Pos"] [:th {} "Number"] [:th {} "Competitor"] [:th {} "NOC"] [:th {} "R1"] [:th {} "B Final"] [:th {} "Final"] [:th {}] [:th {}] [:th {}]]] [:tbody {} [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {} "1"] [:td {:class "bib"} "177"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/athletes/47512"} "Kristin Otto"]] [:td {} [:a {:href "/countries/GDR"} [:img {:style "padding-right: 2px; vertical-align: middle", :src "https://olympedia-flags.s3.eu-central-1.amazonaws.com/GDR.png"}] "GDR"]] [:td {} "55.80 (2 h8)"] [:td {} "–"] [:td {} "54.93 (1)"] [:td {} [:span {:class "Gold"} "Gold"]] [:td {}] [:td {}]] [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {} "2"] [:td {:class "bib"} "88"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/athletes/46122"} "Zhuang Yong"]] [:td {} [:a {:href "/countries/CHN"} [:img {:style "padding-right: 2px; vertical-align: middle", :src "https://olympedia-flags.s3.eu-central-1.amazonaws.com/CHN.png"}] "CHN"]] [:td 